window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-b81d7ecf0390ca3e"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"personalize-chatgpt\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"chatgpt\">个性化 ChatGPT</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整的文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>你可以对 ChatGPT 进行个性化设置，让它的回答和工作方式更符合你的偏好。你可以控制启用哪些个性化功能，也可以随时在设置中更改。网页端和桌面端提供的控制选项可能不同。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-a-personality-on-the-web\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">在网页端选择个性风格</h2> <p>在 ChatGPT 网页端，打开 <strong>Settings &gt; Personalization &gt; Base style and tone（设置 &gt; 个性化 &gt; 基础风格与语气）</strong>，选择 ChatGPT 的回答方式。个性风格会改变它的风格与语气，但不会改变它的能力。</p> <p><a id=\"add-custom-instructions\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">添加自定义指令</h2> <p>你可以使用自定义指令告诉 ChatGPT 需要在不同对话中持续遵循的偏好，例如你喜欢的回答风格。在 Codex 中，这类个人指令存储在全局 <code>AGENTS.md</code> 文件中。项目和代码库也可以提供各自的指令。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-94f17e3de1ca7cb3\">了解 <code>AGENTS.md</code> 指令的工作方式</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"match-your-writing-style-in-work\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"work\">让 Work 采用你的写作风格</h2> <p>在网页端的 ChatGPT Work 中，写作风格功能会参考你在已连接应用中的文字，帮助草稿听起来更像你。</p> <ol> <li>打开<a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/?surface=work&amp;writing_style=setup\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">设置写作风格（需联网）</a>。</li> <li>连接你希望 ChatGPT 使用的电子邮件、消息或文档应用。可用的应用取决于你的账户和工作区。</li> <li>选择 <strong>使用写作风格（Use writing style）</strong> 来启用此功能。仅连接应用并不代表完成设置。</li> <li>请 Work 起草电子邮件、消息或文档。</li> </ol> <p>若要关闭此功能，请在网页端打开 <strong>设置 &gt; 个性化 &gt; 写作</strong>，然后关闭 <strong>参考我的写作风格（Reference my writing style）</strong>。你也可以从同一位置返回设置流程。</p> <p><a id=\"carry-context-forward-with-memories\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">使用记忆延续上下文</h2> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">记忆</a>可以把先前对话中的有用上下文带到后续工作中。记忆可以包含稳定的偏好、重复使用的工作流程、项目约定，以及其他原本需要你反复说明的背景信息。</p> <p>记忆与必须遵循的项目指引不是一回事。必须始终生效的指令应放在 <code>AGENTS.md</code> 或已纳入版本管理的项目文档中。</p> <p><a id=\"add-recent-activity-with-computer-history\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">使用计算机历史记录补充近期活动</h2> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-f3a0216fc3d2956b\"><strong>计算机历史记录（Computer History）</strong></a> 是 macOS 桌面端的一项可选功能。启用后，它可以根据允许使用的应用和网站中的活动生成记忆与时间线。它会利用交互事件，以及 macOS 辅助功能所提供的文本和其他上下文；不会把屏幕截图加入历史记录，也不会录制音频。</p> <p>启用前，请先查看计算机历史记录会收集哪些内容。你可以暂停此功能、排除应用和网站、查看或删除单条时间线项目，也可以随时清除近期记录或全部历史记录。</p> <p><a id=\"manage-personalization\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">管理个性化设置</h2> <p>打开 <strong>设置</strong>（已阻止不安全链接），即可更新个人指令、记忆及其他可用的个性化设置。日常偏好设置的概览请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-1e04f0e469568257\">ChatGPT 桌面应用设置</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"personalize-chatgpt\">Personalize ChatGPT</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Personalize ChatGPT so its responses and working style better match your preferences. You control which personalization features are enabled and can change them in settings. Available controls vary between web and desktop.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-a-personality-on-the-web\">Choose a personality on the web</h2> <p>On ChatGPT web, open <strong>Settings &gt; Personalization &gt; Base style and tone</strong> to choose how ChatGPT responds. A personality changes its style and tone; it doesn't change its capabilities.</p> <h2 id=\"add-custom-instructions\">Add custom instructions</h2> <p>Use custom instructions for preferences you want ChatGPT to follow across chats, such as your preferred response style. In Codex, these personal instructions are stored in your global <code>AGENTS.md</code> file. Projects and repositories can also provide their own instructions.</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-94f17e3de1ca7cb3\">Learn how <code>AGENTS.md</code> instructions work</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"match-your-writing-style-in-work\">Match your writing style in Work</h2> <p>In ChatGPT Work on the web, writing style uses your own writing from connected apps to help drafts sound like you.</p> <ol> <li>Open <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/?surface=work&amp;writing_style=setup\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Set up writing style (online)</a>.</li> <li>Connect the available email, messaging, or document apps you want ChatGPT to use. Available apps depend on your account and workspace.</li> <li>Select <strong>Use writing style</strong> to enable it. Connecting an app alone doesn't complete setup.</li> <li>Ask Work to draft an email, message, or document.</li> </ol> <p>To turn it off, open <strong>Settings &gt; Personalization &gt; Writing</strong> on the web and disable <strong>Reference my writing style</strong>. You can return to setup from the same section.</p> <h2 id=\"carry-context-forward-with-memories\">Carry context forward with memories</h2> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">Memories</a> let ChatGPT carry useful context from earlier chats into future work. They can include stable preferences, recurring workflows, project conventions, and other context you would otherwise need to repeat.</p> <p>Memories are separate from required project guidance. Keep instructions that must always apply in <code>AGENTS.md</code> or checked-in project documentation.</p> <h2 id=\"add-recent-activity-with-computer-history\">Add recent activity with Computer History</h2> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-f3a0216fc3d2956b\">Computer History</a> is an opt-in macOS desktop feature that can turn activity across allowed apps and websites into memories and a timeline. It uses interaction events, along with text and other context available through macOS accessibility features. It does not include screenshots in your history or record audio.</p> <p>Review what Computer History includes before enabling it. You can pause it, exclude apps and websites, inspect or delete individual timeline items, and clear recent or all history at any time.</p> <h2 id=\"manage-personalization\">Manage personalization</h2> <p>Open <strong>Settings</strong> (blocked unsafe link) to update your personal instructions, memories, and other available personalization controls. See <a href=\"#/article/a-1e04f0e469568257\">ChatGPT desktop app settings</a> for an overview of everyday preferences.</p>"};
